  "claims": [
    "New conversational projections preserve the exact parent claim qualifier, version, source references with declared reliability, and recorded contradiction references. This occurs at publication or derived-index repair, not by foreground archive traversal. Candidate content/identity and suppression fingerprints remain unchanged.",
    "Missing or ambiguous claim grounding and oversized qualified projections remain inspectable records but do not enter conversational context. Caveats are never truncated to fit. Actual authenticated ordinary input tests observe the source notes.",
    "Additive migration 40 marks legacy projections unqualified. Foreground reads exclude them until bounded 128-row repair reconstructs source notes from the current scoped pinned parent. Records and previous migration digests remain unchanged; real pre-40 database upgrade is exercised.",
    "The repair index includes only qualification_revision=0 rows, preserving the full-text-first selection plan. Runtime background maintenance performs one approximate 16-page FTS merge chunk per call; no unbounded optimize command runs in runtime or normal selection. The synthetic corpus setup drains those same maintenance chunks before measurement.",
    "Final local 100/10000/100000-record benchmark passes all local gates with 1800/1800 expected enabled details, zero deadline misses. At 100000 records, selection p95 is 0.083 ms warm, 0.105 ms with the synthetic background writer, and 0.286 ms with a new database connection; OS caches are not flushed. These are local host lookup measurements only."
  ],
