  "retainedFailures": [
    "Initial non-partial qualification index made Node SQLite choose a qualification-first plan. The 100-record corpus failed local gates; the 10000-record run was deliberately interrupted after a separate copied-database query reproduced 11528.997 ms before index correction versus 1.259 ms afterward. Initial progress log and exact Node query-plan diagnostic are retained; no completed raw report exists for the interrupted run. Python SQLite used a different plan and was not used as evidence of Node behavior.",
    "Partial index alone preserved all expected details but 100000-record p50 selection remained about 6 ms due to FTS fragmentation after repair. Full failed report retained. An isolated diagnostic found optimize reduced 10000-record p50 from 1.154 ms to 0.024 ms; runtime uses bounded merge steps instead. Final merged corpus report retained separately.",
    "Initial storage regression used an ungrounded candidate text differing from its parent; corrected the fixture to provide its asserted source claim. New unresolved-grounding negative remains.",
    "Initial full regression exposed stale migration health expectations and a sparse-ledger fixture that applied the new ALTER then erased its ledger entry. Readiness now includes 40; legacy sparse test starts from pre-40 schema. Final full suite and 34 focused migration/server tests pass.",
    "Initial private validation identified a stale LS-MEM-093 definition digest. Reviewed mapped acceptance cases, added exact source-projection/legacy/oversize assertions to LS-TEST-125, refreshed the digest, and passed final validation."
  ],
